    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Nasim Nunez** anchors our offensive approach with a strong 64.14 efficiency score. Despite his assumed #8 spot in the order, he faces a favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner (5.10 xERA), with his profile further bolstered by a 19% boost from the SP skill differential. While we are prioritizing SB efficiency, **Sam Antonacci** is our next most intriguing start; his #1 spot in the lineup against Kumar Rocker provides a 10% order boost, keeping him just shy of the \"Strong\" threshold at 59.34. **Tommy White** and **Jackson Merrill** offer solid mid-tier output, with **Tommy White** benefiting from a 10% park factor, while **Jackson Merrill** utilizes a positive dynamic platoon adjustment to offset his matchup against the tougher Braxton Ashcraft.\n\nThe roster configuration is heavily dictated by the absence of our core sluggers\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014all of whom are sidelined by team off-days, effectively forcing our depth pieces into the spotlight. Among our active players, **Liam Hicks** carries the most risk; his 49.04 score is tempered by a significant -11% penalty for a left-on-left platoon disadvantage against Framber Valdez. We are currently leaning on the optimizer's projection for **Miguel Vargas**, who holds a respectable 54.64 score, though his utility slot production remains contingent on maintaining his assumed #3 spot in the lineup.\n\nWith every hitter currently marked as \"Lineup Pending,\" our situational scores are fluid. The most precarious situation involves **Liam Hicks**, where a late-breaking lineup adjustment pushing him down the order could necessitate a pivot to **Drake Baldwin** or **Dominic Smith** if they are active. We are prioritizing speed and lineup position today to maximize our chances in the SB category, keeping a close eye on **Nasim Nunez** to provide the necessary stolen base upside against a vulnerable arm in Ryan Feltner. Should **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, or **Coby Mayo** see a promotion to the starting nine, we remain prepared to adjust our daily game cap management accordingly.",
